commit cd6ec99064b5c1f810f861ce5f51d7b05eafbd30

C03: a literal request to delete a named file in a known folder is the recoverable known-file trash (FILES1241 repair)

«borra el archivo hola.txt del escritorio», «borrá el archivo viejo.txt»,
«delete old.txt from the desktop», «mandá a la papelera …» read as
filesystem.known.trash.named with fileName and folder (desktop/documents/
downloads, or all_known when none is named; the provider refuses ambiguous
names). A bare name must look like a file or the request must say
«archivo/file»; «borra el mensaje», «borra todo», prohibitions and compounds
stay outside. Offline recogniser baseline: four literals gain a reading, none
lost. No tests (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


